## Day 22 – Starting “Product Demand Analytics”

![](https://github.com/omolola-A/120-days-data-analytics-journey/blob/main/Day-22-IMG.png)

After completing my first unguided Excel project, I started a new one: Product Demand Analytics.

The business problem is more strategic this time — unstable month-over-month revenue, unpredictable demand across warehouses and regions, and limited visibility into product and geographic performance.

Today was groundwork.

I went through the dataset carefully to spot abnormalities and inconsistencies, made necessary corrections, and began structuring the data. Inserted Pivot Tables, outlined the core KPIs, and mapped out the time intelligence measures I’ll need to track revenue volatility and demand trends properly.

No dashboard yet. Just structure, clarity, and direction.

The more I do this, the more I realize the real work starts before any chart is built. Next step: stress-test the assumptions behind the volatility. 

